**WELCOME TO LARK CAMP {{ camp_year }}!!**

## COVID and Lark Camp

There is no longer a vaccine requirement. All Campers must present a negative Covid test taken within the 48 hours before camp and are strongly encouraged to test as close to arrival as possible. Any over-the-counter test is fine, as is a timed photo of it. Do NOT email us a photo.

If you test positive for COVID just before camp, text or email us (707) 397-5275 or [registration@larkcamp.org](mailto:registration@larkcamp.org), to say you are not coming; we will refund your money if you need to cancel for COVID-related reasons. If you develop symptoms while at camp, some test kits will be available for purchase at the camp offices. If you test positive for COVID at camp, please report to camp staff promptly.

Everyone attends camp at their own risk. Updates based on CDC recommendations may be sent out shortly before camp.

## Arrival at Camp

Detailed directions are here: [Getting to Lark Camp](https://www.larkcamp.org/about/#Getting_to_Lark_Camp)

Registration opens at 3:00 pm, {{ opening_day | date('%A, %B %-d, %Y') }} (noon on Tuesday for 2nd Half campers). Campers and Instructors: Please do not arrive at camp before 3:00 pm on Friday unless you have been confirmed as an early arrival on a work crew or to help with registration. A limited number of volunteers are needed to arrive early and help with registration. If you would like to do this contact [registration@larkcamp.org](mailto:registration@larkcamp.org)

Note that Vehicle Registration forms and Waivers will now be completed at Registration. Paper forms are no longer sent.

## Departure from Camp

The 1st half campers need to depart before noon/lunch on Tuesday. Full campers and 2nd half campers need to depart before 9am on Saturday morning. We block the road with a trailer to dismantle the Dance Pavilion in Camp 1 starting Saturday morning at 9am, so if you are still in camp you'll be blocked from leaving until 11am and conscripted to help break down camp.

If you plan on leaving a day early, please let us know when you register so that we have an accurate census for the campsite.

## If you are new to Lark Camp...

We suggest arriving early (that is, anytime after 3:00 pm) to have time to get settled in before it's dark in an unfamiliar place. Have a look at this detailed list of things to bring to camp: Michael's Ridiculously Simplified Lark List.pdf

Bring acoustic instruments. There is little facility for electric instruments at camp.

**Newcomer Orientation sessions at Camps 1 & 2**  
Saturday 8:30 am & Tuesday 6:00 pm (both camps)

* Camp 1: Meet at the steps outside the office
* Camp 2: Meet at the inner fire circle by the Coffeehouse

